  {
    "id": "dvcc-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "DVCC charge taper",
    "disabled": true,
    "info": "Tapers the DVCC charge current limit as the highest cell voltage\napproaches the alarm threshold. Prevents weak cells from overshooting\nduring DESS balancing charges that top up to 100%.\n\nSetup:\n1. Review MAX_AMPS and taper thresholds in the taper calc function\n   (your DVCC MaxChargeCurrent is currently 50 A — the flow will\n   override it dynamically between MIN_AMPS and MAX_AMPS)\n2. Enable this flow tab and deploy\n\nThe victron-output-ess node writes to the DVCC charge current limit\nat Settings/SystemSetup/MaxChargeCurrent. The victron-input-battery\nnodes read MaxCellVoltage and SOC from your Pylontech stack via the\nCAN bus data already on the Cerbo."
  },
